### ActiveMQ end-to-end demo (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Prerequisites: ActiveMQ :61616, WorkloadApplication :8082, GymRestApplication :8081
### IMPORTANT: Seed data already has John.Doe and Mike.Brown — demo uses Amy.Coach / Sam.Member instead.
### Run requests top-to-bottom. Tokens/passwords are saved automatically between steps.
###
### Quick links (browser, no auth unless noted):
###   Gym CRM Swagger:  http://localhost:8081/docs
###   Gym CRM health:   http://localhost:8081/actuator/health
###   Workload health:  http://localhost:8082/actuator/health
###   ActiveMQ console: http://127.0.0.1:8161/admin  (admin / admin)
###
### No IntelliJ license? Run: http\run-activemq-demo.bat

@host = http://localhost:8081
@workloadHost = http://localhost:8082

### 0) Health checks (optional)
GET {{workloadHost}}/actuator/health

###
GET {{host}}/actuator/health

### 1) Register trainer (NOT Mike.Brown — that name already exists in seed data)
POST {{host}}/trainers/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Amy",
  "lastName": "Coach",
  "specialization": "Cardio"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("trainer_username", response.body.username);
    client.global.set("trainer_password", response.body.password);
    client.global.set("trainer_password_encoded", encodeURIComponent(response.body.password));
    client.global.set("trainer_token", response.body.token);
    client.log("trainer_username=" + response.body.username);
    client.log("trainer_password=" + response.body.password);
%}

### 2) Register trainee (NOT John.Doe — that name already exists in seed data)
POST {{host}}/trainees/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Sam",
  "lastName": "Member",
  "dateOfBirth": "1998-05-12",
  "address": "Tbilisi"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("trainee_username", response.body.username);
    client.global.set("trainee_password", response.body.password);
    client.global.set("trainee_password_encoded", encodeURIComponent(response.body.password));
    client.global.set("trainee_token", response.body.token);
    client.log("trainee_username=" + response.body.username);
    client.log("trainee_password=" + response.body.password);
%}

### 3) Assign trainer to trainee — use {{trainee_username}} / {{trainer_username}} from steps 1-2
PUT {{host}}/trainees/{{trainee_username}}/trainers
Authorization: Bearer {{trainee_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "traineeUsername": "{{trainee_username}}",
  "trainersList": [
    { "username": "{{trainer_username}}" }
  ]
}

### 4) Add training — usernames MUST match variables from steps 1-2 (not hardcoded John.Doe)
POST {{host}}/trainings
Authorization: Bearer {{trainee_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "traineeUsername": "{{trainee_username}}",
  "trainerUsername": "{{trainer_username}}",
  "trainingName": "Morning Cardio",
  "trainingDate": "2026-08-29",
  "trainingDuration": 60
}

### 5) Verify workload (async - wait 1-2 sec if needed)
GET {{workloadHost}}/workload/{{trainer_username}}/2026/8
Authorization: Bearer {{trainer_token}}

> {%
    client.log("trainingSummaryDuration=" + response.body.trainingSummaryDuration);
%}

### 6) Full trainer workload summary
GET {{workloadHost}}/workload/{{trainer_username}}
Authorization: Bearer {{trainer_token}}

### 7) Optional: login again with saved password
GET {{host}}/login?username={{trainee_username}}&password={{trainee_password_encoded}}

> {%
    client.global.set("trainee_token", response.body.token);
%}
